==Polish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|sla-pro|pl}} {{m|sla-pro|*volxъ}}, itself taken from {{cog|gem-pro|*walhaz|t=Roman, Romance}}. Cognate with {{cog|en|Vlach}}, {{m|en|Wallachia}}, {{m|en|Wales}}, {{m|en|walnut}}.<ref>Rebecca Posner., ''The Romance Languages: A Linguistic Introduction'' (New York, 1966), p. 271</ref>

